 "story": "Counted three riders leaving, two stragglers left behind. \nSun's dropping, beans still in the pot-nobody hungry yet, but they will be.\n\nNothing much to do now except listen for laughter, \nwatch the shadows get long, \nand wonder if there's enough salt for what's coming.\n\nIt's always the waiting that tastes the strongest, \nlong before the supper bell ever rings.",
 "notes": "Rather than focusing on action or spectacle, the portrait centers on the quieter roles that sustained frontier life. The cook's relaxed posture, apron, and boots suggest a figure whose work happened just outside the drama of the trail yet remained essential to it. Subtle backlighting and shallow depth separate him gently from the background, allowing the textures of clothing and weathered features to carry the narrative.\n\nThe composition echoes the observational character studies common in early documentary and Western portrait traditions, where everyday figures were given the same visual weight as the heroes of the trail. The result is a contemplative study of patience, routine, and the understated authority that came from experience earned over many seasons of camp life.",
