 "story": "They say every wanted poster leaves out the best parts.\n\nYou can call me outlaw, hero, fool-it's all the same once the ink dries. I've walked farther and waited longer than most men ever will, and there's more truth in these scars than any bounty notice could print.\n\nThis is my story. You want the rest? You'll have to hear it from me.",
 "notes": "The upright stance and quiet confidence of the figure recall the visual language of classic Western portraiture, where posture alone suggests character and history. The tree anchors the composition while the rifle and gun belt introduce the subtle tension between labor, survival, and legend.\n\nSoft monochrome toning and shallow depth keep the background subdued, allowing the figure's silhouette and gesture to carry the narrative weight. The result feels less like a posed portrait and more like a moment of stillness along the frontier trail, where presence and reputation often spoke louder than words.",
